{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 25, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e2b-it", "content": "Arthur awoke to the familiar scent of pine and damp earth, but something felt…off. The sunlight streaming through the trees wasn't quite right, too perfect, too vibrant. He sat up, a strange tingling sensation spreading through his limbs. He glanced down and saw not his own worn pajamas, but intricately detailed leather armor. A small, ornate sword was strapped to his hip. Panic flared as he looked around. The forest surrounding him was rendered with impossible detail, every leaf and pebble meticulously placed. He tried to speak, but his voice came out as a clipped, slightly accented phrase, something he’d heard countless times in fantasy novels. This wasn't his life. He was in a video game.\n\n***\n\nA shimmering, translucent message appeared before him, hovering in the air like a digital notification. \"Welcome, Player 734. You are now in Aethelgard. Your objective: defeat the Shadow Lord and restore balance to the realm. Good luck.\" Arthur stared, dumbfounded. The message was crisp, coded, undeniably artificial. He instinctively reached for the sword, testing its weight. It felt real, solid. A guttural roar echoed through the trees, and a hulking, grotesque creature with glowing red eyes emerged from the undergrowth. It was clearly designed, a perfect enemy encounter. Arthur knew, with a sickening certainty, that his adventure had just begun, and it was far more perilous than any game he’d ever played.\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "Arthur", "logprob": -0.7662928104400635}, {"token": "▁awoke", "logprob": -0.5493413209915161}, {"token": "▁to", "logprob": -0.002990300301462412}, {"token": "▁the", "logprob": -0.007507680915296078}, {"token": "▁familiar", "logprob": -1.6050341129302979}, {"token": "▁scent", "logprob": -0.623042106628418}, {"token": "▁of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁pine", "logprob": -0.25282976031303406}, {"token": "▁and", "logprob":